/**
 * Federated identity and delegated login via external OAuth 2.0 / OIDC and SAML providers.
 *
 * <p>
 * This bounded context manages the integration with external identity providers (IdPs). It
 * orchestrates the full delegated-login flow: selecting the appropriate provider, building the
 * outbound authentication request, receiving and validating the provider's response, mapping
 * external identity claims to a local user, and handing control back to the Authentication context
 * so that a regular OIDC session and token set can be issued. It acts as an Anti-Corruption Layer
 * between external IdP protocols and the internal authentication model.
 *
 * <p>
 * <b>Key domain types:</b>
 * <ul>
 * <li>{@code DelegatedAccessExternalProvider} — provider interface (Strategy) that each external
 * IdP implements: {@code request(details)} builds the outbound redirect or POST, and
 * {@code authenticate(details, params)} validates the provider response and returns the asserted
 * {@code FederatedUser}, or nothing.</li>
 * <li>{@code PendingDelegation} — a login started by one browser: tenant, client, provider,
 * server-built return URL, PKCE verifier, SAML request ID and the hash of the browser binding.
 * Stored under the hash of its {@code state} and consumed once.</li>
 * <li>{@code DelegatedRequestDetails} — values sent to and expected from the provider (callback
 * URL, state, code verifier, request ID).</li>
 * <li>{@code FederatedUser} — identity asserted by a provider: stable subject, email and whether it
 * is verified. Accounts are reached by subject, never by display name.</li>
 * <li>{@code DelegatedProviderDescription} — UI-facing descriptor for a provider button.</li>
 * <li>{@code DelegateLoginGateway} — composite port: providers of a tenant, pending login storage
 * and account resolution. {@code FederatedIdentityGateway} keeps the links (provider, subject) to
 * users.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p>
 * <b>Key application services:</b>
 * <ul>
 * <li>{@code DelegateLogin} — starts a login bound to the browser and completes it once: consumes
 * the pending login, checks binding, tenant, client and provider, asks the provider to validate its
 * response and resolves the local account.</li>
 * <li>{@code FederatedIdentityWithinOneTenant} — rejects links between a user and a provider of
 * another tenant in the Access API.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p>
 * <b>Infrastructure adapters:</b>
 * <ul>
 * <li>{@code GoogleDelegatedAccessProvider} — Google OIDC with state and PKCE; identity from the
 * UserInfo {@code sub}.</li>
 * <li>{@code SamlDelegatedAccessProvider} / {@code SamlResponseValidator} — SAML 2.0 SP-initiated
 * SSO with strict response validation (signature, issuer, audience, destination,
 * InResponseTo).</li>
 * <li>{@code DelegatedAccessAuthValidatorAdapter} — provider registry and account resolution by
 * link policy; {@code FederatedIdentityAdapter} — links on {@code user-federated-identity}.</li>
 * <li>{@code DelegateRepositoryJdbcAdapter} — pending logins in
 * {@code _oauth_delegated_state}.</li>
 * <li>{@code DelegatedStep} / {@code DelegatedAccessController} — HTML driver: start from the login
 * form and provider callback forwarding to the authorize step.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p>
 * <b>Internal structure:</b>
 *
 * <pre>
 * delegatelogin/
 * ├── domain/
 * │   ├── DelegatedAccessExternalProvider.java  — provider Strategy interface
 * │   ├── PendingDelegation.java / DelegatedRequestDetails.java / FederatedUser.java
 * │   ├── DelegatedAccessDescriptor.java / DelegatedProviderDescription.java
 * │   ├── gateway/   — DelegateLoginGateway, DelegatedStoreGateway, DelegatedAccessProviderGateway,
 * │   │                FederatedIdentityGateway
 * │   └── provider/  — GoogleDelegatedAccessProvider, SamlDelegatedAccessProvider,
 * │                    SamlResponseValidator
 * ├── application/
 * │   ├── DelegateLogin.java            — federated-login orchestrator
 * │   └── listener/FederatedIdentityWithinOneTenant.java
 * └── infrastructure/driven/
 *     ├── DelegateLoginAdapter.java / DelegateRepositoryJdbcAdapter.java
 *     └── DelegatedAccessAuthValidatorAdapter.java / FederatedIdentityAdapter.java
 * </pre>
 *
 * <p>
 * <b>Dependencies:</b> Invoked by the Authentication context through the delegated login steps.
 * Depends on the Access model (users, login providers, federated identities).
 *
 * <p>
 * <b>Stability:</b> moderate; provider implementations evolve as new IdPs are integrated. The
 * domain model and orchestrator are stable; the provider strategy isolates IdP-specific protocol
 * details from the rest of the flow.
 */
